=== layout: one-panel

# Meiosis I is Unique

@body

- Three events are unique to meiosis, and all three occur in meiosis l
  - Synapsis and crossing over in prophase I\: Homologous chromosomes physically connect and exchange genetic information
  - Homologous pairs at the metaphase plate
  - Separation of homologs during anaphase I


@notes

Source: lect06c-meiosis.odp, slide 49.

=== layout: multiple-choice

@question

The diploid number of a roundworm species is 4. Assuming there is no crossover, and random segregation of homologues during meiosis, how many different possible combinations of chromosomes might there be in the offspring (not including variety generated by crossing over)?

- A) 4
- B) 8
- C) 16
- D) 64

@answer

[Answer\: C]{color=red}

@notes

Source: lect06c-meiosis.odp, slide 50. Replacement reason: normalized overlapping legacy components into one native source-order panel; unrecognized source text color #ff00cc requires review

=== layout: multiple-choice

@question

The diploid number of a roundworm species is 4. Assuming there is no crossover, and random segregation of homologues during meiosis, how many different possible combinations of chromosomes might there be in the offspring (not including variety generated by crossing over)?

- A) 4 possible gametes (no fertilization)
- B) 8
- C) 16 possible offspring (= 4 x 4; after fertilization)
- D) 64

@answer

[Answer\: C]{color=red}

@notes

